 are symmetric, I'm comparing the expected outcomes of candidate policies, and a policy where both pass yields two years each.\n\nI'm checking the expected values of each policy: pass-pass gives 2 years, submit-pass averages 2.5, and submit-submit gives 4, so pass comes out best for both. The subjunctive dependence is imperfect, but the framework still has both copies computing the same policy, so I'm treating it as settled. I'm also questioning whether the 50/50 prior over roles holds up, since conditioning would change the result, though the essay rules that approach out.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm weighing a policy-level decision under P-FDT, since both copies of the model run the same reasoning on different inputs. Because the two prisoners are symmetric, I'm comparing the expected outcomes of candidate policies, and a policy where both pass yields two years each.\n\nI'm checking the expected values of each policy: pass-pass gives 2 years, submit-pass averages 2.5, and submit-submit gives 4, so pass comes out best for both. The subjunctive dependence is imperfect, but the framework still has both copies computing the same policy, so I'm treating it as settled. I'm also questioning whether the 50/50 prior over roles holds up, since conditioning would change the result, though the essay rules that approach out.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":8961,"completion_tokens":1008,"total_tokens":9969,"cost":0.056004,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.056004,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.035844,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.02016},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":449,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}